{# Kubeconfig for *observation only*. Three inputs, all of them named in the design:
     1. the API server URL and the cluster CA — public cluster data, taken from the
        operator's kubeconfig on the orchestration host (the same file the CT106 layer
        reads) because the CA cannot be guessed and must not be rotated in two places;
     2. the credential — the read-only ServiceAccount token from `paperclip-observer`
        (`flux-system`, RBAC in tazlab-k8s), which the operator inserted into the agent
        store. The cluster-admin credential that the *source* kubeconfig carries is never
        read and never copied: only two of its fields are used.
   The token is written into this file (not referenced through an exec credential plugin)
   because the provisioning-time render is the shape that works with no warm gpg-agent
   (P4 §2.2); the file is mode 0600 on the data volume and owned by the service user.
   Rotation is therefore: re-insert `agent/k8s/token`, re-run the playbook. #}
apiVersion: v1
kind: Config
clusters:
  - name: tazlab-k8s
    cluster:
      server: "{{ paperclip_k8s_server }}"
      certificate-authority-data: "{{ paperclip_k8s_ca_data }}"
users:
  - name: paperclip-observer
    user:
      token: "{{ paperclip_k8s_token }}"
contexts:
  - name: paperclip-observer
    context:
      cluster: tazlab-k8s
      user: paperclip-observer
      namespace: flux-system
current-context: paperclip-observer
preferences: {}
